# Build artifacts and dependencies at ANY depth: a bare pattern only matches
# the context root, so packages/web/.next, packages/core/dist and every
# packages/*/node_modules would otherwise enter the image layers. Both
# Dockerfiles run `bun install` inside the image, so host copies are never
# needed (and could shadow the linux-native install).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.next-e2e
**/.next-e2e-ui
**/coverage
**/coverage-tmp
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.DS_Store
# Editor/agent worktrees and caches (.claude/worktrees holds full checkouts of
# other branches — ~1GB of context the images must not carry).
.claude
# Match .env-family secrets at ANY depth. A bare `.env` only excludes the
# context root, so deploy/selfhost/.env (created by the quickstart) would
# still be COPYed into the pew-selfhost:local image — leaking real secrets
# into an image layer. `cp .env .env.bak` must not reopen the hole.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
**/.dev.vars
**/.rqlite-auth.json
deploy/selfhost/*.auth.json
# Local wrangler/miniflare state (D1 emulation caches; git ignores them, the
# images must too — deploy/selfhost/Dockerfile copies packages/worker whole).
**/.wrangler/
# Backup archives and their staging dirs (backup.sh output; the archive holds
# every password_hash/api_key, and build contexts are the repo root, so a
# build running while an archive exists would bake it into an image layer).
**/backup-*.db
**/.pew-backup.*/
logo.png
scripts/resize-logos.py
